Our Why At Dotmatics&nbsp;

At Dotmatics, a Siemens company,&nbsp; we believe science, data, and decision-making must be deeply intertwined for innovation to thrive. Our Portfolio includes Luma, LumaLab Connect, ELN Platform, Graphpad Prism, Geneious, SnapGene, Protein Metrics, OMIQ, FCS Express, LabArchives, NQuery, EasyPanel, SoftGenetics and Virscidian.

We have a vision for a new Lab of the Future that will change the future of scientific research.

We have created the world’s most comprehensive digital science platform - best-of-breed software applications already used by more than 2 million scientists, together in a single ecosystem united by a powerful, flexible enterprise data platform. This is not flat data buried away in digital graveyards. This is dynamic, multi-dimensional decision-making.

Scientific enterprises need a new level of effectiveness to achieve tomorrow’s breakthroughs. Illness will not wait. The biosphere will not wait. We are tireless in our vision, because the time for innovation is now.

Shaping the Future of Science At Dotmatics&nbsp;

Our global team of more than 800 colleagues are dedicated to supporting our customers in over 180 countries. Together, with our scientific community of users, we accelerate scientific innovation in order to make the world a healthier, cleaner, and safer place to live.

You’ll join a collaborative, global team pushing the boundaries of scientific innovation.&nbsp; Your ideas and efforts will have a tangible impact, accelerating scientific progress and discovery. We offer a dynamic, remote-friendly environment that fosters high integrity and collaboration, empowering you to excel. Dotmatics is a company built by scientists, for scientists. Combined, we are now the world’s largest cloud-based scientific research R&amp;D platform. We need your help to keep growing and pioneering the future.

We are Science Driven. We are Customer Centric. We are Better Together.&nbsp;

What do we need  &nbsp;

We are looking for a Senior Project Manager to manage large Scientific SaaS delivery &amp; implementations projects, to ensure that our clients are reaching their desired outcomes and adopting our solutions. The structure of projects are like other enterprise deployments but centre around enabling Customers to use configured software within their business area of expertise. &nbsp;

You will be in a unique position to leverage your advanced  in-depth SaaS Implementation/delivery skills, processes management, and interpersonal skills across many clients, ranging from the top pharmaceutical companies in the world to the leading food providers, and start-ups focused on ultra-rare diseases. You will be an advocate of Dotmatics, engaging stakeholders ranging from bench scientists up to Senior Manager levels to effectively communicate Actions, Owners, Timelines, to balance risks and have the right conversations to protect, propose, and allow science to prosper. &nbsp;

In this role you will get to &nbsp;

• Develop, plan and manage the implementation of challenging Customer projects across disparate organizations in line with the Dotmatics project lifecycle using agile methodologies and hybrid-agile approaches. &nbsp;

• Lead full cycle project delivery for complex enterprise level SaaS software &nbsp;

• Manage large technical &amp; digital transformation programmes &nbsp;

• Develop project objectives, by identifying requirements and barriers to projects, including cost, time, scope, and resources. &nbsp;

• Lead resolutions of any customer or team problem related to their discipline/project. &nbsp;

• Proactively identify problems that challenge our scale or business or customer direction. &nbsp;

• Effectively communicate and support changes to adapt to challenges by taking accountability for the project’s success. This may require working across a number of different aspects, e.g. equipment, business processes, vendor management, technical implementation, deployment and training. &n

